        {
          "id": "e1841bc0-ec72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
          "name": "2. FARMSTEAD",
          "label": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">2. FARMSTEAD</p></div>",
          "order": 2,
          "complete": false,
          "description": null,
          "tooltip": null,
          "imageUrl": null,
          "questions": [],
          "subchapters": [
            {
              "id": "51ece562-4c63-f011-bec2-002248afff4e",
              "name": "CHAPTER 2 BUILDINGS AND ROADS",
              "label": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Buildings and Roads</strong></p></div>",
              "order": 2.1,
              "complete": false,
              "description": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">On most farms, the yard, buildings and access roads are the heart of day‑to‑day work. How you place, build and maintain them can protect water, soil, air and habitat—and also reduce complaints from neighbours. Roofs, paved yards and roads change how rain runs off your land, which can lead to erosion or flooding if not managed well. Stream crossings and work near ditches or creeks can affect fish and wildlife. This section explains these risks in plain terms and shows you how to manage them.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Planning ahead pays off. This chapter points to the rules that may apply to your farm and reminds you to factor in climate risks like wildfire and heavy rain that can raise flood risk. Smart siting, drainage, and construction choices can lower those risks and protect your operation for the long term.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">If you’re completing an Environmental Farm Plan, use this section alongside support from an EFP Planning Advisor. Walk your yard after a storm to see where water flows, note any crossings, and check whether building locations and roads are working with—not against—your land and neighbours.</p></div>",
              "tooltip": null,
              "imageUrl": null,
              "parentChapterId": "e1841bc0-ec72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
              "questions": [],
              "subchapters": []
            },
            {
              "id": "0c70869d-3063-f011-bec3-000d3a0c38d2",
              "name": "CHAPTER 2 CHEMICAL FERTILIZER",
              "label": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Chemical Fertilizer</strong></p></div>",
              "order": 2.2,
              "complete": false,
              "description": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Fertilizers help crops grow, but if they’re not handled properly, they can harm water, soil, and air. Extra nutrients can wash into streams and lakes, causing algae blooms and fish kills. Spills or poor storage can also contaminate drinking water. Some fertilizers, like ammonium nitrate, are even a fire risk if stored near fuel or heat sources.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">This section explains how to store, handle, and apply fertilizers safely. You’ll learn about the rules that apply in B.C. and practical steps to reduce risk—like keeping fertilizers away from wells and ditches, using proper containment, and applying the right amount at the right time.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Good fertilizer management saves money and protects your land. It also helps you meet environmental standards and avoid complaints from neighbors. If you’re working on your Environmental Farm Plan, use this section with your Planning Advisor to check your current practices and plan improvements.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">The goal is simple: keep nutrients where your crops need them and out of places they don’t belong.</p></div>",
              "tooltip": null,
              "imageUrl": null,
              "parentChapterId": "e1841bc0-ec72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
              "questions": [],
              "subchapters": []
            },
            {
              "id": "c801a189-4c63-f011-bec2-002248afff4e",
              "name": "CHAPTER 2 FARM WASTE",
              "label": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>FARM WASTE</strong></p></div>",
              "order": 2.3,
              "complete": false,
              "description": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Every farm produces waste—old fencing, plastic, used oil, animal health products, and more. If these materials aren’t managed properly, they can pollute soil and water, harm wildlife, and create safety hazards. Burning or dumping waste in the wrong place can also break the law and damage your reputation.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">This section covers the main types of farm waste and how to deal with them responsibly. You’ll find tips on reducing waste, reusing materials, and recycling where possible. For items that can’t be reused, we explain safe disposal options, including permitted landfills and take-back programs for things like paint and pesticides.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Managing waste well isn’t just about compliance—it’s about protecting your farm and community. It reduces fire risk, keeps harmful chemicals out of the environment, and shows customers you care about sustainability.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">If you’re completing an Environmental Farm Plan, walk through this section with your Planning Advisor. Together, you can identify problem areas and set up a plan that works for your operation.</p></div>",
              "tooltip": null,
              "imageUrl": null,
              "parentChapterId": "e1841bc0-ec72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
              "questions": [],
              "subchapters": []
            }
          ]
        },
