        {
          "id": "a9ab491a-ed72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
          "name": "6. NUTRIENT APPLICATION",
          "label": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">6. NUTRIENT APPLICATION</p></div>",
          "order": 6,
          "complete": true,
          "description": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><div class=\"ck-content stickystyles-wrapper-insert\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;font-size:11pt;\" dir=\"ltr\" data-wrapper=\"true\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Applying nutrients to your farm—like manure, compost, or fertilizer—is essential for growing healthy crops. But how and when you apply them matters.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">One key approach is the “4R” method: using the Right Source, at the Right Rate, at the Right Time, and in the Right Place. This helps you match nutrients to your crop’s needs while reducing waste and environmental risks.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Check out <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/farming-natural-resources-and-industry/agriculture-and-seafood/agricultural-land-and-environment/environmental-farm-planning/efp-reference-guide/chapters/rg-chp6.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BC's EFP Reference Guide Chapter 6</a> for practical tips for managing manure, choosing soil amendments, and planning nutrient applications throughout the year.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">Whether you’re growing forage, berries, vegetables, or tree fruit, this chapter helps you make informed decisions that benefit your farm and the land around it.</p></div></div>",
          "tooltip": null,
          "imageUrl": null,
          "questions": [],
          "subchapters": [
            {
              "id": "b2a16a4e-4d63-f011-bec2-002248afff4e",
              "name": "CHAPTER 6 NUTRIENT APPLICATION",
              "label": "NUTRIENT APPLICATION",
              "order": 6.1,
              "complete": true,
              "description": "<div class=\"ck-content\" data-wrapper=\"true\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"--ck-image-style-spacing: 1.5em; --ck-inline-image-style-spacing: calc(var(--ck-image-style-spacing) / 2); font-family: Segoe UI; font-size: 11pt;\"><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong><u>Nutrient Sources and the Environment: what you need to know</u></strong><br>&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Why nutrients matter</strong><br>Plants need nutrients to grow. Those nutrients come from fertilizers, manure, soil amendments, and nitrogen fixed by legumes. Each source behaves differently in soil and water—and each can create risk if over‑applied or poorly managed.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Understand the basics</strong><br>This section explains how nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium work, and why soil pH and salts matter. It also covers secondary nutrients, micronutrients, and metals, plus the difference between nutrient sources and soil conditioners.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Watch for problem areas</strong><br>Learn how to avoid phosphorus build‑up, check amendments for contaminants, and choose the right material for your fields.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Plan with confidence</strong><br>Pair this section with tools like the Nutrient Management Calculator and your EFP Planning Advisor to keep nutrients where crops need them and out of waterways.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong><u>Nutrient Application: the 4R basics</u></strong><br>&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Start with the 4Rs</strong><br>Right Source, Right Rate, Right Time, Right Place—this section shows how to apply these principles on your farm.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Match source to crop and soil</strong><br>Choose the right product for your crop and conditions.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Set a rate you can defend</strong><br>Use soil tests and realistic yield goals to avoid over‑application.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Time it to crop demand</strong><br>Apply nutrients when plants can use them. Split applications may help for long‑season crops.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Place to protect water</strong><br>Position nutrients so crops get them and waterways don’t.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Check your work</strong><br>Calibrate spreaders and sprayers, and use post‑harvest nitrate tests to see if your plan worked.</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0;\"><strong>Know the rules</strong><br>This section also summarizes B.C. regulations and setbacks for nutrient application.</p></div>",
              "tooltip": null,
              "imageUrl": null,
              "parentChapterId": "a9ab491a-ed72-f011-bec2-000d3a0c38d2",
              "questions": [],
              "subchapters": [
                {
                  "id": "a884b5c6-4d63-f011-bec2-002248afff4e",
                  "name": "Nutrient Application (Manure, Fertilizer, Compost, etc.)",
                  "label": "Nutrient Application (Manure, Fertilizer, Compost, etc.)",
                  "order": 6.11,
